{
  "what_this_is": "How Trillion runs the configured capability probes and retains exactly what each probe checked, read by src/capability-checks.mjs (the scheduler source `capability-checks` and tool:check-everything-still-works). A check is one of the person's own records, `record:capability-check:<check>`, shown as a row of the list `list` (the screen /lists/<list.id>). A check names a probe (one of Trillion's own tools by `tool` with its `input`, asked inside the person's store exactly as their AI would ask it), the facts it reads from the answer (`facts`: each { id, kind, path, read }, `kind` a formula-engine kind and `read` one of `reads` below), while its answer is still being worked out (`pending_when`, a long tool run still going: read again after `recheck_after_minutes`, nothing counted), when it applies (`in_use`, a formula-engine rule tree over those facts, or null for always) and what a working answer looks like (`expect`, a rule tree over the same facts, operators from parts/formula-engine/rules/rule-operators.json). A probe may also be `account_probe` with { action, input }: one of Trillion's own behaviors in the account (records/workshop-account-tool-records.json, invoke.action), run in the store as every plan includes it. A probe's input may name the day, hour or minute it runs ({checked_on}, {checked_hour}, {checked_at}), so one long run a day is asked by the same key until it answers and a quick read is asked afresh. A path is a list whose items are keys, indices, or { match: { path, equals } } (the first item of a list whose value at path equals). A check runs every `every_hours`; one that fails is checked again `recheck_after_minutes` later, and once it failed `failures_before_handing_off` times in a row it is a stop src/keep-running.mjs acts on (kind check_failed): one AI is handed the fix with the evidence and the person is told, once per stop. `starters` are the checks Trillion offers every account (tool:check-everything-still-works add_starters: true keeps the ones missing and never changes a check the person or their AI changed); each names the change that shipped the capability it checks (`shipped_in`). Adding a check is a row here or one `add` to the tool; nothing in the code names a tool, a fact or an app.",
  "account_probe": "account_action",
  "most_per_wake": 12,
  "recheck_after_minutes": 10,
  "failures_before_handing_off": 2,
  "good_before_working": 2,
  "problem_chars": 600,
  "row_type": "capability-check",
  "reads": {
    "value": "the value at the path",
    "count": "how many items the list at the path holds",
    "hours_since": "how many hours ago the time at the path was"
  },
  "states": {
    "working": {
      "label": "Working"
    },
    "failing": {
      "label": "Failing"
    },
    "not_in_use": {
      "label": "Not in use"
    },
    "not_checked": {
      "label": "Not checked yet"
    }
  },
  "words": {
    "recovering": "Answering again ({good} of {needed} good answers in a row before it counts as working)",
    "no_answer": "{tool} gave no answer it could read: {error}",
    "missing": "The answer from {tool} had no {facts}.",
    "not_expected": "{tool} answered, and it is not what working looks like: {read}.",
    "said_all": "{working} of {total} configured checks passed. These checks cover their declared probes, not every user outcome.",
    "said_failing": "{failing} of {total} configured checks are failing: {labels}.",
    "unknown_check": "There is no check {check_id}. The checks are: {ids}.",
    "bad_check": "A check needs check (letters, digits and dashes), label, probe { tool, input }, facts [{ id, kind, path, read }] and expect (a rule tree over those facts); {why}.",
    "pending": "Still being worked out"
  },
